Z||000016||BBBAD GT||06-22-2000||01:51 PM||||Wow, didn't mean to get anybody "looney" with this, but I was thinking of more so with this Forum (it gets a little more personalized that way).  But if you want the biggest event in history, I say go for it.  <P>BTW, just for reference, the Dragstrip we rented was an NHRA track, for 9 hours with ambulance and track prep and a couple workers, worked out to be around $1.3k.  Its not cheap, and most places (not this one thank god) want at least half up front a couple months in advance.  When you start talking money and how much you need up front.......you'll be surprised how many people tend to drop off (not flaming anybody here, just poiting out our experiences).<BR>||||reg||1
