Z||000021||ThatRickGuy||06-22-2000||06:20 PM||||In a year, I'd actually be able to make it. 12 more months and a few days and I no longer have to wear green everyday! I'd say illinois. it's littlerally smack dab in the middle. And there's gotta be some tracks in the area that would be up for a few days of easy cash. I'm originally from WI, so a drive down to even southern Ill would only be like 8 hours. I'd even go if I were from the east coast (12 hour drive err so) if it weren't for the "green machine"... Next year, southern midwest, sounds good to me.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000022||Old Lar||06-22-2000||07:25 PM||||Although Watkins Glen is a nice track and only a hour and a half from me, the Hotel/motel of the area is rather sparse.  There would be no host hotel.  There are great wineries in the area, Seneca Lake boat rides, the area is rather isolated.  Its a very scenic area of New York State.<P>Cost of track rental is probably out of sight.  FOCOA had the track at Gateway International.  It was $5K, I think.  $50/per person, if they got 100 people.  Too many said it was a great idea, I want to particpate, up until the money needed to pass hands.  Then it was too expensive.  If you want to get a track they will want the money up front, so someone will need deep pockets to front the cost and then hope, the wannabes come up with the cash at the right time.<P>I hate to be a downer, but planning events for too many of the Fiero world is a losing proposition.  You read the posts:  I want to put a big block V8 in my Fiero, but I don't have any money.  I need a new exhaust system, but I don't have any money.<P>The people who put on the shows at Daytona, the Dells, Carlisle and all the others put in a lot of time and effort in planning these events and it is the same few people year after year.  It is expensive to go to the shows.  Gas, food, tolls, hotel, etc. & time.  You add up the cost.  Do you have the money?||||reg||9
