Z||000053||RiceCooker||06-23-2000||07:11 PM||||Some are concerned with $$$ and distance. I for one would like to say that these are legitimate concerns , but this isn't something that comes along often. It's probably once in a lifetime. I would certainly not drive for 30+ hours to go to a fiero show in the states somewhere. But if there is something on a scale such as this, i'm sure myself and many others would be willing to make sacrifices. I'm not trying to say that I love fieros more than anyone else but i'm 19, live in western canada, and i'd be thrilled to come!<P>Just my $0.02||||reg||1
Z||000054||RiceCooker||06-23-2000||07:36 PM||||By the way, HAZE does not get to make the sign.<P>R-A-L-L-E???-Y||||reg||7
Z||000055||stimpy||06-23-2000||07:50 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by elfiero:<BR><B>HELLO! AREN'T YOU PEOPLE LISTENING?IF IT'S EAST OF THE MISSIPPI, ONLY 1/2 THE PEOPLE<BR>ARE GOING TO SHOW UP! BUT MAYBE THATS WHAT YOU WANT OR JUST DON'T CARE[EVEN WORSE] HOW 'BOUT ST LOUIS? IGNORING ME ISN'T GONNA MAKE ME GO AWAY.<P>P.S. FYI THE THREE STATES WITH MOST REGESTERED FIEROS ARE FLORIDA,MINNESOTA,<BR>MICHIGAN.IN THAT ORDER!THINK ABOUT IT WHEN PICK'IN A SITE.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I think this kind of rant is an adequate reason to forget about the whole thing. No offense intended, elfiero, but there is no solution that will make everyone happy. I feel that effort is far more productively expended on improving your LOCAL Fiero club. Don't got one? Make one. Find out where a neighboring club meets, drive out and visit them and encourage grassroots collabaration. That is just my opinion, but I think it has more potential for success then a nationwide meet in it's first year.<P>If my pissin on the parade does not dissuade those enthusiastic about this noble venture, may I make a location suggetion? Branson, MO. It is central, Very scenic ith plenty of ty mounain roads, an abundance of cheap lodging, and things to do for the grouchy old farts of the forum who can actually afford to take off many days to drive cross country.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000056||Old Lar||06-23-2000||07:50 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">  Elfiero take a pill.  I drive my Fiero all over.  I drove to KC after the Dells and got some good barbeque at the Smokestack of Martin City.  Everyone, wont be driving equal distances no matter where the planned show is cause, those that live in Topeka wont be driving two days to get to Topeka.<P>FOCOA was in St Louis in 98, were you there?I drove two days to get there, so much for us easteners driving.  There were others who drove even further that I did from east of me.  Parrenti came in from California, Fiero Doc came in from California.  There are lots of people that come to the midwest shows.<P>The Michigan club got most club participants at the Daytona show this year.<P>"If you build it, they will come"||||reg||1
Z||000057||FieroWife||06-23-2000||08:19 PM||||When Old Lar mentioned the Wisconsin Dells before, an idea hit.  Milwaukee has a thing every year around the fourth of July called, "Summer Fest".  A ton of bands (popular ones, not just locals) come in for a week and play in one central outdoor location.  That would give everyone something else to do also.  Wisconsin isn't exactly the middle of the country but there would be one more really cool thing for everyone to do.  Also, if it's done around the Fourth, many of us would have a freebie day anyway.  Just my $.02.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000058||webbee||06-23-2000||09:55 PM||||Good idea about piggy backing on another event. <P>I vote for the KS option as I'm in So. CA. I drove from Houston to LA and my butt still hurts.<P>Don't know if my car will be ready. however.||||reg||14
Z||000059||Haze_Performance||06-23-2000||09:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B>Tell you what - I can set up another one of those polls to see which place something like this could be held. That way, it's a democratic decision... First I'd need all options ofcourse.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>OPTION 1. Route 66 Raceway (Illinois)<P>||||reg||14
Z||000060||batboy||06-23-2000||11:44 PM||||I work right next to Heartland Park in Topeka, Kansas and you'll NEVER see me volunteering to help out with this event. You guys have no idea how much work it takes to pull a big event off. Usually one or two people do ALL the work and everyone else complains. If you have started planning and working on it now, something might be ready by next summer. Lots of folks already have vacation plans worked out this summer. The only time I know for sure you could use the dragstrip at Heartland Park this summer is during Grudge Nights on July 28 or September 8, and I doubt you could reserve the road course at this late notice. That would be expensive too. We might just have to split it up into several regional get-to-gathers. Like US east coast, US midwest, US west coast, Canada, and Europe. Those two or three members over in Hawaii will have a pretty small gathering. The Alaska members might have to drive to the Canadian event or organize their own too. It gets very complicated very quickly.||||reg||1
