Z||000067||BAM-BAM||06-24-2000||11:14 AM||||  Ok, here's what you do. Take a ruler and measure from the lowest southern tip of the US to the highest northern point in Canada (civilized of course)and half that. Measure from the western most point, on the west coast to the eastern most point, on the east coast and half that. Plot these two respective points on the map of the western hemosphere, BAM! there's where you have your gathering. As for those of you on the European Continet, Hawaii and possibly Alaska, you all could have similar but localized events. We tend to eliminate our brothers to the north in our calculations. But really who cares where it is? Plan for a couple three days of meeting and sharing with over 1000 Forum friends (some not so friendly). Where ever you have it, must have some kind of convention facilities. After that it would be up to the "Event Organizers" to arrange smaller events. Sort of the microevents of the macroevent. I'm Sure that there could be arrangements for vendors and suppliers to be there, afterall, this would truely bring the bulk of the market right to them. I would hate to see such a wonderfull idea ruined by a few whiners and snivelers. How ever this comes off, if it comes off, some will be lucky, others, not so lucky. It's the spirit of the thing that matters. Could you imagine ove 1000 people in one place, all with such a inique commonality? It would be AWESOME!! Alrigh now, let's all take a deep breath and come up with two or three "CENTRALLY" located options (with the infrastructure) and have a DEMOCRATIC vote on wich is best. I believe Cliff mentioned that he could arrange such a thing given the choices. The hardest part of this whole thing is moving forward from here. Once a lacation is agreed upon, then we can see what kind of number we are dealing with.<P> Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smilysun.gif">  ||||reg||8
Z||000068||batboy||06-24-2000||01:32 PM||||For the record, there are not 1000 active Forum members. We've asked Cliff about this in the past. Since there is not an easy way to deactivate member status, lots of those members included in the total may of vanished a year ago or at least months ago. It would be safe to say that only about half that number are probably currently active members. Still, that's a lot of people spread out over a very large geographical area.||||reg||1
Z||000069||Haze_Performance||06-24-2000||04:03 PM||||I think that the concept of a Hugh gathering is great. But before we all start arguing on when and where, we should have a vote. Cliff can you put up a poll we can vote on? The poll should be “Will you travel to a Central US Fiero Event?? Yes or No.. “ Then we will know who’s in and who’s out.   <P><BR>Thanks<BR>Carl ||||reg||14
Z||000070||Archie||06-24-2000||05:26 PM||||I hope you guys would like to hear another opinion. There are already several "Regional" events put on every year by some of the larger clubs. Some of them are very big and well run multiple day events. One such event is The Dells Run put on by the Wisconsin Fiero Fanatics. Several other area clubs such as NIFE, the MN club, and clubs from IA & MI & IN. This event is a full 3 days of things to do including a car show, a cruise, a golf outing, sight seeing, seminars and a rally. This show has been going on for like 9 years or more and it is totally organized with scheduled events taking place on schedule and as planned. More than 200 people and 130+ Fieros showed up this year for the Dells show.<P>Earlier Batboy tried to explain to you how difficult (& thankless) organizing such an event would be. Please don't underestimate just how much effort it takes to put together  a successful event. I can Guarantee you that for every 10 people who volunteer to help only one will actually show up when you need him.<P>My suggestion would be to get hooked up with one of the existing successful shows, like the Dells show, and work with their existing organization to find a local racing venue to be added to their existing 3 or 4 days of Fiero events.  You know they already have a successful event staff that knows what thier doing and they most likely will welcome a few new events and more attendees.<P>If you want to have a successful event, deal with successful people.<P>Archie<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000071||BAM-BAM||06-24-2000||05:43 PM|||| Good point Archie. That would take alot of the logistical nightmare out of the whole proccess. Com'on y'all lets get it toghether. I want to go! Iwant to go!<P> Bye, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pimp.gif">    ||||reg||10
Z||000072||87GTBro||06-24-2000||05:55 PM||||If money is ever a concern, look at the number of registered members on the forum.  We have 1162 members...  Make it 1000 to include dead accounts.<P>If everyone donates $10, the grand total would be $10000.  $10 sounds like a reasonable price to me.  <P>I personally don't care where this event is because I live right at the southern most tip of the United Stated and I would have to drive more that 1000 miles to get there anyway.  (It takes 600 miles just to get out of Texas the short way!)<P>Now the only problem is finding someone honest enough and with enough integrity to be the treasurer...||||reg||4
Z||000073||deceler8||06-24-2000||06:46 PM||||I say we all meet at the docks in Fort Lauderdale, load our cars on the ferry to Freeport, Bahamas, and terrorize the locals by driving on the left side of the road (they drive on the right, and not too well...)<P>Everything you could want...beaches, casinos, cheap liquor...about a three hour boat ride from Ft. Lauderdale.<P>Maybe instead of an international event, we should have an international incident...||||reg||1
Z||000074||Old Lar||06-24-2000||08:41 PM||||Archie has the right idea..tag along with the established regional shows ot even the national show.<P>The Pontiac Oakland Club International (POCI) is having it convention in Grand Rapids  7/11-15.<P>I went to it last year in Buffalo, and there were only 14 Fieros at the show.  You need to belong to POCI, but wouldn't it be great if the Fiero world swarmed to a POCI convention?<P>||||reg||7
